  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued unbound in double corrugated boards hand torn and stained with ink. Nine pages are overlaid with linoleum cut illustrations; three are overprinted with text; all on hand-made Indian rag and wheat chaff paper with torn edges. The whole is held together with baling twine.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Artist's book by Lisa Corinne Davis, in which she explores the idea of female African American identity through layered complex linoleum cut portraits.</subfield>
    <subfield code="b">Portraits of African American women are overprinted with iconic images of white women of art history, including a Madonna and Child, a Rembrandt woman, Botticelli's Venus, and Alice in Wonderland as drawn by John Tenniel.  The figures also represent the various ages of a woman, from infant (Madonna and Child), young girl (Alice), mature woman (Botticelli's Venus), and old woman (Rembrandt's "83-year old woman").</subfield>
  </datafield>
